From 1b54869be3df64af0cd192055ab7b5303181e12b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:26:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 32/39] drama: --voices serves voice files and --default-voice
 picks one

--voices DIR reads every regular NAME.json voice file at startup: names are
checked, links, directories and hidden files are skipped, and a file whose
transcript the reference would refuse or whose codes miss codes_sha256 stops
the start. A request's voice names one; --default-voice NAME is used when it
names none. tools/zig/drama_voice.py writes voice files with the pinned
reference's own encode of a references[].audio_path (load_audio, then
FishReferenceEncodeHook in bfloat16 on CUDA).
